$DIR/test.p:3:2: assignment mismatch: 2 variables but atoi(s) returns 1 value besides the error
    In an or statement, the values of the call are its results other than the
    last, which is the error that the clause tests. The left side needs one
    operand for each value, and err, which the clause declares, is not one of
    them.
    (see "Assignment statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.7)
    (run "pluto explain E0017" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/test.p:4:2: assignment mismatch: 1 variable but fail() returns only an error; write it without a left side
    In an or statement, the values of the call are its results other than the
    last, which is the error that the clause tests. This call returns only an
    error, so it has no values to assign: write the statement without a left
    side.
    (see "Assignment statements" in the Plutonium spec, section 12.7)
    (run "pluto explain E0017" for a longer explanation)

$DIR/test.p:5:2: assignment mismatch: 3 variables but two() returns 2 values besides the error
    (explained above; run "pluto explain E0017" for more)
